<title>USA: U.S. Feb single-family home sales fell 0.7 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Feb single-family home sales fell 0.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Commerce Department reported sales of new single-family homes, seasonally adjusted, with percent changes from prior month (numbers in 1,000s).</p>
<p> -		 Pct--Feb    Jan-(Prev)    Dec-(Prev)</p>
<p> Total Units  -0.7  811    817   870     789   801</p>
<p> -By Region:   Pct--Feb    Jan-(Prev)    Dec-(Prev)</p>
<p> - Northeast -11.2   95    107   134	76    82</p>
<p> - Midwest    -3.4  141    146   140     156   156</p>
<p> - South	-3.4  364    377   403     351   360</p>
<p> - West	 11.7  210    188   192     205   204</p>
<p>Total February sales of single-family homes rose 4.2 percent from an annualized rate of 778,000 units a year ago.</p>
<p>    In 1,000s:	Feb     Jan--(Prev)    Dec--(Prev)</p>
<p> Actual Units Sold   67	60     64	51     51</p>
<p>Sales Prices:</p>
<p> --Mean	     174.5   170.2  172.8   171.5  171.3</p>
<p> --Median	   143.2   143.8  145.0   142.9  143.0</p>
<p>Note-Actual number of new single-family units sold is not seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>Wall Street economists forecast February single-family home sales at a seasonally adjusted annual rate of 811,000 units.</p>
<p>The department also revised monthly percent changes of total sales, seasonally adjusted, from prior months as follows:</p>
<p>    -	     Jan-(Prev)   Dec-(Prev)   Nov--(Prev)</p>
<p> Total Units    3.5   8.6    0.1   0.5   11.6   12.9</p>
<p>The annualized sales rate for November was revised to 788,000 units from 797,000.</p>
<p> Number of Months:     Feb    Jan-(Prev)   Dec-(Prev)</p>
<p> -Supply of Homes	4.6    4.8   4.5    5.1   5.0</p>
<p> 1,000 Units:	    Feb    Jan-(Prev)   Dec-(Prev)</p>
<p> -End-Month Inventory  312    316   314    322   322</p>
<p>The department said the 4.6 months supply of homes at the current sales rate in February was the lowest since 4.5 months in December 1993. It also said that the February decline in sales was the first since October last year.</p>
</text>
